<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="sec-mathematical-finance">
<title>Mathematical Finance</title>

<introduction>
<remark>
<title>Prerequisites</title>
<p>Probability, statistics, stochastic processes, stochastic calculus,
differential equations, optimization, linear algebra, numerical methods,
and mathematical modeling.</p>
</remark>

<remark>
<title>Learning Objectives</title>
<p>By the end of this section, the reader should be able to:</p>

<p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>explain the purpose of mathematical finance;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>distinguish assets, securities, portfolios, and derivatives;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>compute simple and continuously compounded returns;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>distinguish arithmetic and logarithmic returns;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>understand discounting and compounding;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>compute present and future values;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>understand discount factors;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>recognize yield and interest-rate conventions;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>understand bonds and zero-coupon securities;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>compute bond prices from discounted cash flows;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>understand duration and convexity conceptually;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>define financial risk and return;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>compute portfolio expected return;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>compute portfolio variance and covariance;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>understand diversification;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>formulate mean-variance portfolio optimization;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>recognize the efficient frontier;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>understand minimum-variance portfolios;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>understand the role of correlations in diversification;</p>
